course: dictionary
lesson: 9800
title: A holy text called a sutra
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A sutra is a holy teaching or text. You can work out this meaning from the clues around the word. «The Diamond Sutra, a Buddhist holy text printed in 868 AD» tells you that a sutra is a holy text, and Buddhist tells you which religion it belongs to.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The Diamond Sutra, a holy teaching printed in 868 AD» still makes sense, so your meaning fits the context.
explain: The second sentence gives more clues. «It is now in the British Library in London» tells you that sutras are valuable, old books that people keep and look after. Clues like these help you understand a word you have not met before.
fact: A sutra is a holy teaching or text in Buddhism or Hinduism.
fact: Monks in Buddhism chant sutras, which means they say or sing them aloud.
fact: «The Diamond Sutra» was printed in 868 AD and found in a cave at Dunhuang.
fact: «The Diamond Sutra» is the oldest dated printed book in the world.
fact: In Hindu learning, a sutra can also be a short rule or saying that is easy to remember.
exercise: «The Diamond Sutra, a Buddhist holy text printed in 868 AD, is the oldest dated printed book.» What is a sutra? | A type of cave | A kind of monk's robe | *A holy teaching or text | A printed newspaper
exercise: Sutras belong to which two religions? | *Buddhism and Hinduism | Judaism and Hinduism | Judaism and Christianity | Sikhism and Islam
exercise: «It is now in the British Library in London.» Where is the Diamond Sutra kept now? | In a temple in Lhasa | In a cave at Dunhuang | *In the British Library in London | In a school in Delhi
test: «The Diamond Sutra» was printed in which year? | 1,100 AD | *868 AD | 1850 AD | 1200 AD
test: In Hindu learning, a sutra can also be what? | *A short rule or saying that is easy to remember | A type of drum | A long song | A kind of wooden block
exam: Which is the best meaning of sutra? | A type of cave painting | *A holy teaching or text in Buddhism or Hinduism | A kind of wooden block for printing | A famous river in India
